Package: observer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: dhtech <dhtech@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dhtech/observer
Description: sees a network as a visitor's computer does, for Prometheus
 observer acts as a visitor's computer on one network interface: it
 asks for an address over DHCPv4 and DHCPv6, asks name servers a
 question and pings targets, again and again, and serves what it saw
 as Prometheus metrics on port 9023.
 .
 One static binary and the unit observer.service. A first installation
 neither enables nor starts it: it needs its settings first
 (OBSERVER_OPTS in /etc/default/observer, at least -interface).
